.TH SENTINEL-DUMP 1 "March 2026" "Sentinel-CC v4.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sentinel-dump \- Sentinel-CC policy inspector
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sentinel-dump
[\fI\-\-json\fR] \fIBINARY\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sentinel-dump
reads and pretty-prints all Sentinel-CC embedded sections from an ELF
binary. It displays the syscall whitelist policy, CFI caller-range
metadata, imported external functions, and signature status.
.PP
This tool is useful for verifying that the LLVM compiler pass correctly
instrumented a binary, auditing which syscalls and call-sites are
whitelisted, and confirming signature status before deployment.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
Print version string and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Output in JSON format instead of human-readable tables. Suitable for
piping into \fBjq\fR or other JSON processing tools.
.SH SECTIONS DISPLAYED
.TP
.B .sentinel
Syscall policy entries. Each entry maps a call-site address to a
syscall number and function address. Shows virtual addresses, file
offsets, and resolved syscall names.
.TP
.B .sentinel_cfi
CFI caller-range metadata. Each entry maps a syscall call-site
to the function that is allowed to contain it, enabling deep CFI
enforcement.
.TP
.B .sentinel_imports
List of external (libc) functions the binary calls. Used by the
loader for call-graph BFS to compute transitive syscall reachability.
.TP
.B .signature
Ed25519 signature over .text, .sentinel, .sentinel_cfi, and
.sentinel_imports. Shows size, type detection, and signing status.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Sections dumped successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Error (no Sentinel sections found, file not readable, ELF parse failure).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Inspect a signed binary
sentinel-dump ./victim_phase2

# JSON output piped to jq
sentinel-dump --json ./victim_phase2 | jq '.sentinel | length'

# Check if a binary is signed
sentinel-dump ./myapp | grep "Status:"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sentinel-loader (1),
.BR sentinel-sign (1),
.BR readelf (1)
